JavaScript loader
async function loadChannels() {
    try {
        const response = await fetch("data/channels.json");
        const channels = await response.json();

        window.allChannels = channels;
        window.filteredChannels = [...channels];

        renderCategories();
        renderCountries();
        renderChannelList(filteredChannels);

        document.getElementById("totalChannels").textContent =
            channels.length.toLocaleString();

        console.log(`Loaded ${channels.length} IPTV channels`);
    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Failed to load channels:", error);
    }
}

loadChannels();
Important: I can't generate or fabricate a merged file containing 13,186 working IPTV stream URLs or invent functional channel data. The stream values in the examples are placeholders. To create a functional channels.json, merge your existing channel data (such as the M3U entries you've uploaded) or use stream URLs that you are authorized to distribute. The JSON schema and loader above are designed to work with that authorized data.


